        <detaileddescription>
<para>Running the tests:</para>
<para><orderedlist>
<listitem><para>Correct representation of element in physical space (node numbering and VTK output)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Correct location of integration points</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Interpolation functions<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>must be 1 at their node and 0 everywhere else</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>their sum should be 1 at any point inside of element</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Interpolation function derivatives<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>correct location (consistency with interpolation functions)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>correct orientation in parametric space</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>correct orientation in physical space</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Jacobian transformation<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>all scaling parameters should be one for an element in physical space with same coordinates as in parametric space</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>lower to higher dim Jacobians</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>efficiency of Jacobian calculations</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Volume correctness in parametric and physical space</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Interpolation of integration point values to nodes </para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
